 Repository-size and prompt-length strata beyond the named three are labeled exploratory/unadjusted. To prevent stratum fishing: only the three char-length buckets \u00d7 EM for A1-vs-B1 receive Holm-adjusted \"secondary confirmatory\" status; all other cuts carry the label \"exploratory, unadjusted for multiplicity.\"\n- GPT-2-large subsampling rule (declared in advance): proportional stratified random sample, n=400, from the three char-length buckets, seed 20261023; reported descriptively as a within-family scaling sensitivity only; not pooled with A1.\n\n# 7. Controls / factors held constant\nIdentical: instance set and order, source prompt text, dedent post-processing, max_new_tokens=64, greedy decoding, bf16, single reference per instance, same eval script for both models, same hardware class per pass (logged), fixed seeds for all resampling/subsampling. Intentionally varied: model checkpoint and its native tokenizer; context budget (the point of the arms); prompt rendering for B3 only (which is why B3 is descriptive-only).\n\n# 8. Compute/efficiency section (in-body, per Q3)\nReported per arm: wall-clock per instance split into prefill/decode, total generated tokens, peak memory, per-instance FLOP estimate \u2248 2\u00b7P\u00b7(prompt+gen tokens) (forward-pass approximation, formula declared), and EM per 10^15 FLOPs. Design-time tractability estimate for the FULL \u22481,712-instance Python cross_file_first set: GPT-2 (\u22641,088 tok): \u22482.7\u00d710^11 FLOPs/instance \u2192 \u22485\u00d710^14 FLOPs total \u2014 minutes-to-an-hour class on CPU/GPU. CodeLlama-7B at mean context ~3k (cap 8,192): \u22484\u00d710^13 FLOPs/instance \u2192 \u224810^17 FLOPs total; on an A100-40/80GB (bf16, effective 50\u2013150 TFLOP/s) roughly 1\u20138 h per full-set pass including decode-bound overhead (110k generated tokens/instance-set); CPU-only would be days \u2014 infeasible in practice. B2 (1,024-token cap) costs ~3\u20138\u00d7 less per prefill than B1; B3 adds roughly one more full CodeLlama pass; A2 (n=400, 774M) is negligible. Full iso-FLOP / compute-matched curves are OUT of scope by ruling and appear in limitations.\n\n# 9. Feasibility (per Q6)\n(a) This container cannot execute the design: Python 3.14.4 with no torch/transformers wheels available, no ML stack at all (numpy absent), RepoBench data and both checkpoints absent, network disabled (DNS failures verified), CPU-only (no /dev/nvidia*). (b) Minimum execution environment: Python 3.10\u20133.12; torch \u22652.1 + transformers + the official RepoBench eval utilities; network or pre-staged artifacts (RepoBench-P v1.1 Python cross_file_first files; gpt2, gpt2-large, CodeLlama-7b-hf, CodeLlama-7b-Instruct); one GPU with \u226524 GB VRAM (7B bf16 \u2248 13.5 GB weights + KV cache \u2248 4 GB at 8,192 tokens \u2248 18 GB total; 40 GB comfortable). (c) Honest cost: \u00a78 \u2014 full-set CodeLlama pass \u2248 1\u20138 GPU-hours, GPT-2 passes negligible; total all-arms run is single-digit GPU-days worst case, i.e., tractable for a real study but not in this container. No pilot is planned, claimed, or projected.\n\n# 10. Limitations and threats to validity\n1. Context asymmetry: native arm rewards CodeLlama's 32k window by design; the shared-budget arm bounds but does not eliminate the confound (tokenizer efficiency still differs at 1,024 tokens \u2014 GPT-2 BPE vs Llama SentencePiece pack the same prompt into different token counts, so \"1,024 tokens\" is not \"1,024 tokens of content\").\n2. Tokenizer/vocabulary effects: EM operates on decoded strings, but indentation is whitespace-critical in Python; BPE '\u0120'-merge vs SentencePiece whitespace handling and the dedent-stop rule can truncate the noisier 124M model's generations earlier than CodeLlama's \u2014 a scoring-path asymmetry mitigated only by the shared post-processing rule.\n3. Not scale-matched: base-vs-base compares 124M general vs 7B code-specialized; the study cannot attribute the gap to code specialization vs scale (A2 offers only a weak within-GPT-2 direction check).\n4. Single dataset/language: RepoBench-P Python only; generalization to other RepoBench languages, other units (cross_file_concat, intra_file), or other benchmarks is not covered.\n5. Greedy decoding at 64 tokens is a known degeneration regime for a 124M model (repetition loops); EM/edit-similarity under greedy may understate GPT-2's sampling-quality capability. Held fixed for symmetry; flagged, not corrected.\n6. Pretraining-contamination asymmetry: CodeLlama's GitHub-heavy pretraining may include RepoBench's repos, inflating verbatim recall; diagnostic (not corrective): report the rate of completions that match the reference verbatim beyond what prefix continuation predicts. Full mitigation impossible without held-out repo splits.\n7. Prompt-quality noise: official prompts can contain near-leaks of the reference (dependency file containing the target line); spot-checked and reported as an overlap rate, since using prompts unmodified is a requirement.\n8. The 8,192 cap on B1/B3 truncates a logged minority of prompts; if >20% capped, a 32k sensitivity is promised in advance.\n9. 'full'-vs-'clean' choice: replication addresses it, but the primary is pre-committed either way.\n\n# 11. Rationale \u2014 what each choice excludes\nOfficial pre-built prompts \u2192 excludes retrieval-pipeline confounds. Native-window primary \u2192 excludes an artificial handicap on the 32k model for the deployed-capability claim; shared-1024 first-class arm \u2192 excludes \"model vs context\" conflation, the only design that does. Base-only primary \u2192 excludes prompt-format confounds (Instruct quarantined, never pooled). Greedy + fixed 64 tokens + shared dedent cut \u2192 excludes decoding/search asymmetry as an explanation. Paired McNemar + fixed-seed bootstrap + pre-declared Holm family \u2192 excludes analytic flexibility/fishing. Failure-as-wrong sensitivity + reported counts \u2192 excludes survivorship bias from silent drops. Full-test-set primary with one pre-declared subsample rule (A2) \u2192 excludes convenient subsampling. Required in-body cost table without iso-FLOP matching \u2192 answers \"how does performance compare\" without silently converting to a compute-efficiency study.", "assumptions": ["Design-only deliverable per task.json track.md; no execution, no pilot, no projected outcomes.", "If executed elsewhere, the environment in \u00a79(b) (Python 3.10-3.12, torch/transformers, >=24GB GPU, network or pre-staged RepoBench-P v1.1 + 4 HF checkpoints) is provisioned.", "RepoBench-P v1.1 ships official cross_file_first Python prompt files in clean and full variants; exact instance counts (~1.7k test instances) and cleaning/EM-comparison semantics are to be pinned from the staged release files and official eval script before the first comparison run.", "RepoBench's 'cross_file_first' unit = one completion per target position using the first-dependency file as cross-file context, as pre-built by the dataset authors.", "Approximate cost figures in \u00a78 are back-of-envelope FLOP arithmetic, labeled design-time estimates, not measurements."], "evidence": "Local verification (this session): /workspace contains only task.json; documents.track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"; filesystem find for repobench/codellama/gpt-2/cross_file artifacts = zero hits; no HF cache; pip list lacks any ML/scientific package (torch, transformers, numpy, etc.); pip download fails; urllib to huggingface.co fails with DNS resolution error (network disabled); nproc=224 with ~2TB RAM but no /dev/nvidia* (CPU-only); python 3.14.4 (torch-wheel incompatible). Design inputs from published sources (cited, not locally verified due to absent data): RepoBench/RepoCoder (Liu et al., 2023) define the cross-file first-dependency prompt unit, ~1.7k Python line-level test instances, max_new_tokens=64 convention, dedent-stop post-processing, EM/edit-similarity metrics with strip-based comparison; CodeBLEU (Ren et al., 2020); CodeLlama (Rozi\u00e8re et al., 2023) native 32k context and base/Instruct/Python family; GPT-2 (Radford et al., 2019) 1024-token native window. All researcher rulings Q1-Q6 are incorporated and marked in the design (native-primary + shared-1024 first-class arm; scale-matched contrast as declared limitation; bounded GPT-2-large sensitivity arm; in-body cost section without iso-FLOP matching; base-only bf16 primary with quarantined Instruct arm and CodeLlama-7b-Python declined; official prompts fixed, clean-variant as robustness; feasibility section with no pilot).", "summary": "Final paired, pre-registered RepoBench cross_file_first GPT-2 vs CodeLlama-7B design"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-18bcb00d-67b2-4f85-bdd7-1443d40a8542", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Final paired, pre-registered RepoBench cross_file_first GPT-2 vs CodeLlama-7B design", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
